---
description: when developing, either adding features, changing code, refactoring code and tests.
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Please always check compilation with `cargo check` if any Rust code is changed.

The last step is alwys to run `cargo check --test` to make sure everything is ok.

Please format code frequently.
- run `cargo fmt --all -- --check` before any task is finished

Please add and update unit tests when applicable.

Use the makefiles aliases when appropriate

If any documentation is needed put in /docs, or in README.md if important.

Use curl to verify UI changes

make sure there are no compilation warnings before finishing a task

Delete any unused variables and imports.

Do not suppress unused variable warning by prefixing it with an underscore. Delete unused code.

If any changes needed for testing, make sure the docker image is rebuilt first.

Refactor often. 

Test often. With targeted tests, not whole suite.

Check formatting and linting often.

Prefer small functions ala clean-code, using with shared helpers and libraries.

Do not repeat yourself, use helper functions.
 
Prefer more domain based logic.

Avoid very big files. 

Make small changes, format code, pass tests, iteratively.

- All text should be in message bundles, never in line if possible.

- All message keys should always be translated
